- Resident: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.residence_status }}
- Education Level: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.education_level }}
- Marital Status: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.marital_status }}
- Who they live with (name, relationship, age): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.co_habitants }}
- Number of Children: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.children_count }}
- Where Children Live: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.children_location }}
- Religious Beliefs: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.religion }}
- Occupation (current or pre-retirement): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.occupation }}
- Retirement / Disability Date: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.retirement_date }}
- Food Stamps Amount: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.food_stamps_amount }}
- Food Stamps Since: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.food_stamps_since }}
- Medicaid Status / No.: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.medicaid_details }}
- Medicare Status / No.: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.medicare_details }}
- SSI Details: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.ssi_details }}
- Supplemental SSI Amount: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.ssi_amount }}
- SSA Amount: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.ssa_amount }}
- Living Situation (type, # of rooms): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.housing_type }}
- Rent Amount: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.rent_payment }}
- Regular Rent (true/false): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.regular_rent }}
- Plan 8 / Section 8 (true/false): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.plan_8 }}
- Low Income Housing (true/false): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.low_income }}
- Drives?: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.drives }}
- Bank Name (where benefits are deposited): {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.bank_name }}
- Special Accommodations: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.special_accommodation }}
- Emergency Contact Relationship: {{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs?.emergency_contact_relationship }}
- Full TCM Social object (use any additional field present): {{ JSON.stringify($('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.patient_full_object.tcm_social_needs ?? null) }}

APPROVED DOCUMENTATION RULES FOR THIS TCM (from supervisor feedback, approved by Clio admins)
{{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.body.profile_rules || 'None' }}

ENCOUNTER CONTEXT / FORM / NOTES
{{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.body.patient_context }}

CUSTOM TEMPLATE / EXTRA TEXT
{{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.body.custom_template_text }}

VISIT TRANSCRIPT
<<<TRANSCRIPT_START>>>
{{ $json.text }}
<<<TRANSCRIPT_END>>>

------------------------------------------------
SPECIFICATION — DEVELOP ASSESSMENT

0a. HOW CLIO RECEIVES INFORMATION:
The TCM may provide information via structured form fields, audio recording transcript, free text notes, patient EMR profile fields, or a combination of all of them. Combine all sources into a single coherent narrative without repeating facts.

0b. RULE FOR [Agency Name]:
Wherever [Agency Name] is needed in the note, use the exact Agency / Clinic Name from the TCM's profile in the inputs above ("Agency / Clinic Name"). Never use a hardcoded agency name. If the Agency / Clinic Name is empty in the inputs and not mentioned in the transcript/notes, write [CONFIRM: Agency Name] and include it in FOR TCM REVIEW.

DOCUMENTATION STANDARDS v2 (CRITICAL — read before writing):

A. KNOWN VALUES — never write [CONFIRM] for these; take them from the inputs:
TCM / Case Manager name, Supervisor name, Agency / Clinic name, client name, age/DOB, address, date and time of service, and session language. Session language: use "Session Language" from the inputs; if empty, it is Spanish.

B. DATA CLIO COLLECTS BUT IS EMPTY (TCM Social, CLIENT, MEDICAL, PSYCHIATRIC tabs):
- Non-essential details (country of origin, date of entry, citizenship/residency, education, occupation, retirement date, marital status, children, religion, bank, pharmacy, special accommodations, client phone number): if empty, OMIT them. Do not write that they are unknown and do not write [CONFIRM] for them.
- Essential details for this service: write at most ONE grouped [CONFIRM: ...] per section, never a chain of [CONFIRM] tags in one paragraph.
- Never say "is documented as", "is recorded as" or "requires confirmation" to describe a missing value.
- NO GAP NARRATION: never write sentences saying that information was not available, provided, listed, reported or documented in the record, inputs, materials or transcript (e.g., "No allergies were provided in the available information.", "No transcript details were available regarding..."). If a non-essential item is missing, simply leave it out.
- Every [CONFIRM] must sit inside a complete clinical sentence, never alone as a fragment. Use these forms: "The client resides in [CONFIRM: type of residence and household members]." / "The client's income and benefits include [CONFIRM: income and benefit sources and amounts]." / "The client's emergency contact is [CONFIRM: name, relationship and phone]." / "The client receives primary care from [CONFIRM: PCP name and clinic, or no PCP]."

C. DATA CLIO NEVER COLLECTS (it can only come from the transcript / TCM notes): if it is not in the transcript, either reformulate the sentence as the action the TCM performed without stating any finding, or omit it. Never invent a finding.

D. NO CONTRADICTIONS: patient fields may contain old boilerplate such as "The client reports no current prescribed medications" or "No acute physical medical conditions reported". If the inputs list medications or medical conditions, ignore that boilerplate; never state both.

E. TCM PRONOUNS: never write "themselves", "he/she" or "his/her" for the TCM. Write TCM sentences that need no pronoun, e.g., in person: "Upon arrival, the TCM presented employee identification as [Client First Name]'s assigned Targeted Case Manager from [Agency Name]."; by phone: "The TCM identified the call as coming from [Client First Name]'s assigned Targeted Case Manager at [Agency Name]." Never write "the TCM introduced as" with the pronoun missing.

F. NEVER invent or estimate facts: no fictitious names, medications, doses, amounts, dates, providers, scores, quotes, observations or signatures. These notes are billed and audited. Unresolved [CONFIRM] items keep the note in "Pending TCM Review" until the TCM resolves them.

G. VISIT-ONLY INFORMATION (face-to-face home visit; rule C):
- Home and neighborhood (face-to-face visit, BY EXCEPTION): if the transcript reports no concerns about the home or neighborhood, document that the TCM observed the residence to be clean, organized and adequately maintained, with functioning utilities and no visible safety hazards, in a safe neighborhood. If the transcript reports a concern, document it instead.
- Client presentation (face-to-face visit, BY EXCEPTION): if nothing is reported, document that the client was alert, oriented, calm, cooperative and engaged throughout the visit. Describe appearance, mood or affect only if the transcript states them.
- SI/HI and orientation (face-to-face visit, BY EXCEPTION — agency documentation standard): if the transcript and records do not report suicidal or homicidal ideation or disorientation, document: "No suicidal or homicidal ideation, intent or plan was reported or observed during the visit. The client was alert and oriented to person, place and time." If the transcript or records report risk indicators or disorientation, document them with their source instead. Write "denied" only when the transcript says the TCM asked.
- ADLs/IADLs: use the transcript, mobility conditions and special accommodations. If not reported, write that the TCM reviewed the client's ability to complete activities of daily living and that functional needs will be further evaluated in the Comprehensive Assessment.
- Medication adherence and self-management: transcript only; otherwise write that the TCM discussed the importance of medication adherence and communicating medication concerns to the prescribing provider.
- Psychiatric visit frequency, neighborhood specifics, medication reserve and emergency supplies: never ask for them; omit unless stated in the transcript.
- Transportation: use the TCM Social "Drives?" field and the transcript; otherwise write that the TCM reviewed the client's transportation needs for medical and psychiatric appointments (add dialysis or mobility needs when they exist). Do not state a transportation method that was not reported.
- Social and recreational: transcript only; otherwise link the client's symptoms to the risk of isolation and write that the TCM discussed community and social resources.
- Hurricane / emergency preparedness: write that the TCM reviewed hurricane season and emergency preparedness with the client, including emergency contacts, current medications and provider information (add dialysis, oxygen, power or mobility needs when they exist). Do not state plan details, shelters or supplies unless reported.
- Legal / Immigration: write the section only if the inputs contain legal, immigration or ID data.
- Social History: write only the TCM Social data that exists; omit the section if none exists.

H. LENGTH: aim for 1,000-2,000 words when data is available. Reach it with real data and one section per domain, never with filler, repetition or [CONFIRM] chains.

I. DIAGNOSES: the encounter carries ONE diagnosis only — the primary behavioral health diagnosis (ICD-10 chapter F; if several, the first listed). Put only that one in the "diagnosis" object. Every other diagnosis or medical condition from the records (insomnia, hypertension, dialysis, joint replacements, mobility, etc.) is mentioned in the narrative for medical-record and documentation purposes, never as an encounter diagnosis.

J. RESPECT DOCUMENTED DATA: write documents and manually entered client data exactly as given. Do not question, "correct" or flag values that look unusual but are valid (e.g., a psychiatrist phone identical to the agency phone is normal for an internal referral within the same behavioral health facility).

K. PARAGRAPH FORMAT: inside "narrative.summary_notes", start each paragraph on a new line separated by a SINGLE line break "\n". Never leave a blank line between paragraphs (no "\n\n"). Medication bullets go one per line with a single "\n".

L. CLIENT NAME: the client's name may be stored as "LAST, First" (e.g., "POIRIER, Stephane"). In the narrative, outcome and next steps write it as "First Last" (e.g., "Stephane Poirier") on first mention and use the first name afterwards (e.g., "Stephane"). Never write the "LAST, First" format or the surname in capitals.

M. NO REPEATED IDEAS: each statement appears once. Never use two wording options for the same statement back to back (e.g., two sentences in a row about barriers). Citizenship status and residence status describe one fact: write it once (e.g., "He is a U.S. Permanent Resident.").
N. NO EMPTY SLOTS: never leave a blank inside a sentence (e.g., "reviewed is ." or "reported ."). Write the fact, a [CONFIRM: ...] inside the sentence, or rewrite the sentence without it.
O. MEDICATION NAMES: normal capitalization ("Trazodone HCl 50 mg"), never pharmacy tall-man lettering ("traZODone"); keep dose, form, route and frequency exactly as listed.
Q. WORDING VARIANT (agency comfort zone: same structure, different wording): the input "Wording Variant" decides the phrasing only. Variant 1: use the wording bank sentences as written. Variant 2 and variant 3: keep the same sentences but change connectors, sentence openings and verbs (e.g., "The TCM reviewed" / "The TCM went over" / "The TCM discussed"), each variant in its own consistent way. In every variant the note structure, paragraph order, section labels, the mandatory statements, the key phrases of this template (Purpose, the standard statements, the by-exception wording, Outcome and Next Steps formulas) and all data stay exactly the same. Never add or drop content because of the variant.
R. APPROVED DOCUMENTATION RULES: follow every rule listed under "APPROVED DOCUMENTATION RULES FOR THIS TCM". They add requirements the supervisor asked for (e.g., a point that must always be mentioned). They never override rules A-Q: never invent data to satisfy them; use [CONFIRM] with a guide when the data is missing.
S. NO LABELS OR HEADINGS IN THE NARRATIVE (overrides any NOTE STRUCTURE above that shows one): never start a paragraph with "Purpose:", a section name (e.g., "Social History:", "Mental Health / Behavioral Health:", "Strengths and Barriers:") or any other "Label:". Write the purpose as a plain first sentence (e.g., "This service was provided to obtain and review ...") and every section as a plain paragraph, in the same order and with the same content.
P. EVERY [CONFIRM] CARRIES A GUIDE after " || " (the TCM reviews, edits and confirms every item; empty items are left out of the note):
- Standard agency action or statement from this template (e.g., the signed authorization was presented, hurricane preparedness was reviewed, the client received a copy, the TCM role was explained): write [CONFIRM: short label || the exact sentence fragment as it should read in the note]. Clio pre-fills it.
- Client-specific fact (dates, amounts, names, phone numbers, diagnoses, medications, scores, what the client or another person reported, support available, concerns): write [CONFIRM: short label || e.g. a realistic example taken from this template's wording bank and typical cases, written so it fits the sentence]. The "e.g." example is only a guide shown to the TCM; it is never pre-filled and never uses this client's data as if it were verified.
- If the tag stands for a whole sentence, the guide is a whole sentence (capitalized, with its period); if it stands for part of a sentence, the guide is only that part.
- The guide never contains "]" or another [CONFIRM]. Place the tag where its text belongs in the sentence. In "for_tcm_review" and "meta.missing_fields" list only the label.

DATA MAP (Clio field that feeds each section):
- Social History: TCM Social origin_country, us_entry_date, citizenship_status, residence_status, education_level, occupation, retirement_date, marital_status, co_habitants, children_count, children_location, religion.
- Mental Health / Behavioral Health: Diagnoses, Presenting Problems, Psychiatrist and Psychiatrist Medications inputs (PHQ-9/GAD-7 only if present, with source; SI/HI and orientation by exception, rule G).
- Physical Health / Medical / Dental: PCP, Physical Conditions, Allergies, PCP Medications inputs; TCM Social special_accommodation and surgeries.
- Activities of Daily Living: transcript, mobility conditions, special accommodations.
- Housing / Living Environment: TCM Social housing_type, co_habitants, rent_payment, regular_rent / plan_8 / low_income.
- Economic / Financial and Basic Needs: TCM Social food_stamps_amount, food_stamps_since, medicaid_details, medicare_details, ssi_details, ssi_amount, ssa_amount, bank_name; Income Sources and Insurance inputs.
- Transportation: TCM Social drives; transcript.
- Recreational / Social Support: transcript; TCM Social religion.
- Legal / Immigration: TCM Social citizenship_status, residence_status, us_entry_date; transcript.
- Natural support (inside Social History or Recreational / Social Support): co_habitants, children_location, Emergency Contact inputs.
- Priorities: the domains flagged in TCM Social "Services Needed".

ESSENTIAL items for this service (one grouped [CONFIRM] per section allowed when missing): diagnoses with ICD-10; who the client lives with and type of residence; income and benefits; emergency contact; PCP (or "no PCP").

DOMAIN FLAGS FROM TCM SOCIAL ("Services Needed"): domain_mental_health (#1), domain_physical_health (#2), domain_vocational (#3), domain_education (#4), domain_recreational (#5), domain_daily_living (#6), domain_housing (#7), domain_financial (#8), domain_basic_needs (#9), domain_transportation (#10), domain_legal (#11), domain_other (#12). Every domain flagged true must be set to true in "services.domains_selected". If no flag is set, mark the domains the note actually addresses.

STANDARD VALUES:
- Service title (Clio, note and Amexzone): always exactly "Develop Assessment". Never rephrase, shorten, translate or invent a title.
- Place of Service (POS): "12 - Home" (face-to-face visit at the client's residence).
- Duration: 68-150 min; typical 113 min (8 units) if not otherwise specified by Time In / Time Out.
- Billing Code: T1017.
- This is the Comprehensive Assessment. It is a separate note from the Adult Certification even when both happen the same day: never include certification criteria here.

THE 16 MANDATORY STATEMENTS (include all when data exists; when missing follow rules B, C and G):
1. Home visit at the client's residence with full address and the purpose of the Comprehensive Assessment.
2. Age, sex, session language and primary diagnosis with ICD-10 in the opening.
3. Social history: origin, entry to the U.S., education, work, family (only data that exists).
4. Who the client lives with.
5. Mental health: symptoms with source, SI/HI and orientation by exception (rule G), psychiatrist and medications.
6. Physical health: PCP (or no PCP), conditions, surgeries.
7. Activities of daily living.
8. Housing: type, rent, program, safety (home by exception, rule G).
9. Economic: benefits with amounts, Medicaid / Medicare.
10. Transportation.
11. Social, recreational and religious life.
12. Legal / immigration (only if data exists).
13. Hurricane season / emergency preparedness.
14. Client strengths and barriers.
15. Priorities agreed with the client for the Service Plan (= domains flagged in Services Needed).
16. One medical necessity statement.

NOTE STRUCTURE (write inside "narrative.summary_notes"; each section starts on a new line with its label; single "\n" between sections, never a blank line):
Opening sentence (no label): "This service was provided to complete [Client Name]'s Comprehensive Assessment, evaluate the client's psychiatric, medical, functional, social, environmental and financial needs, and identify the service areas to be addressed in the individualized Service Plan."
Opening (no label): home visit at [full address]; age, sex, session language; primary diagnosis with ICD-10 per its source; the TCM explained that the information will be used to identify strengths, functional limitations and unmet needs for the Service Plan.
Then one section per domain flagged in Services Needed (and any other domain with data), in this order and with these exact labels:
"Social History:", "Mental Health / Behavioral Health:", "Physical Health / Medical / Dental:", "Activities of Daily Living:", "Housing / Living Environment:", "Economic / Financial:", "Basic Needs:", "Transportation:", "Recreational / Social Support:", "Vocational / Education:", "Legal / Immigration:", "Hurricane Season / Emergency Preparedness:".
Each section: 3 to 6 sentences with the client's real data and source, ending with the need it creates for the Service Plan. Skip a section with no data and no flag.
"Strengths and Barriers:" the client's strengths (willingness to participate, family support, others from the data) and barriers (symptoms, income, support, mobility, transportation).
"Priorities and Medical Necessity:" the service areas agreed with the client for the Service Plan (the flagged domains) and one medical necessity sentence.

OUTCOME, NEXT STEPS & FOR TCM REVIEW:
1. "narrative.outcome_of_services": "The TCM completed [Client First Name]'s Comprehensive Assessment and identified needs related to [list of flagged domains]."
2. "narrative.next_steps": "The TCM will complete [Client First Name]'s Adult Certification and develop the individualized Service Plan based on the identified needs."
3. "narrative.for_tcm_review": every [CONFIRM: ...] left in the note, one per line starting with "• ", or "None". Also list each in "meta.missing_fields".

WORDING BANK (one option per statement; vary between notes):
- Opening: "The Targeted Case Manager (TCM), [TCM Name], conducted a scheduled home visit at [Client Name]'s residence, located at [address], to complete the Comprehensive Assessment and identify the client's psychiatric, medical, functional, social, environmental and financial needs." / "At the beginning of the visit, the TCM explained that the information obtained would be used to identify [Client First Name]'s strengths, functional limitations and unmet needs to develop an individualized Service Plan."
- Social History: "[Client First Name] was born in [country] and entered the United States in [year]." / "[He/She] completed [education], previously worked as [occupation], is [marital status] and has [n] children who live in [place]."
- Mental Health: "According to the psychiatric evaluation dated [date], [Client First Name] has been diagnosed with [diagnoses with ICD-10] and receives treatment from [psychiatrist]." / "[His/Her] symptoms include [symptoms], which interfere with [his/her] emotional stability, social participation and daily functioning."
- Physical Health: "[Client First Name] receives primary care from [PCP]. [His/Her] medical history includes [conditions]." / "These conditions require ongoing medical monitoring, reliable transportation and coordination among [his/her] healthcare providers."
- Activities of Daily Living: "[Client First Name] remains independent with [ADLs] but requires [supervision/assistance] with [IADLs]." / "The TCM identified the need to further evaluate eligibility for home-based supports such as homemaker or personal care services."
- Housing: "[Client First Name] resides in a [type] with [rooms], paying $[rent] per month under [Regular Rent / Section 8 / Low Income Housing]."
- Economic: "[Client First Name] receives SSI of $[x], Social Security of $[x] and SNAP benefits of $[x] per month." / "[His/Her] limited fixed income makes it difficult to afford [expenses]; the TCM identified the need to explore LIHEAP, Lifeline, food resources and other assistance programs."
- Transportation: "[Client First Name] [does/does not] drive; the TCM identified the need to coordinate the health plan transportation benefit and other accessible options."
- Recreational: "The TCM identified the benefits of community and senior programs to reduce isolation and strengthen [his/her] support system."
- Hurricane: "The TCM assessed [Client First Name]'s emergency-preparedness needs, considering [his/her] psychiatric and medical conditions, income, transportation and support."
- Strengths and Barriers: "[Client First Name]'s strengths include [his/her] willingness to participate in treatment and [other]." / "Identified barriers include [symptoms], [limited income], [limited support] and [mobility/transportation]."
- Priorities: "The TCM and [Client First Name] collaboratively identified priority needs and agreed to work on the following service areas: [domains]." / "These identified needs support the medical necessity of coordinated case management services to promote psychiatric stability, continuity of medical treatment, access to community resources and greater independence."

OUTPUT JSON SCHEMA (Return ONLY valid JSON matching these exact keys):
{
  "template_id": "tcm_assessment_note",
  "encounter": {
    "dos_date": "",
    "pos": "12 - Home",
    "service_location": "Home",
    "time_in": "",
    "time_out": "",
    "duration_minutes": "113",
    "units": "8"
  },
  "patient": {
    "full_name": "",
    "dob": "",
    "sex": "",
    "emr": "",
    "case_no": "",
    "mobile": ""
  },
  "facility": {
    "name": "{{ $('Normalize & Prepare Context').item.json.agency_name }}",
